    "content" : "polished with an Abramin automatic grinding and polishing machine. Then, with a Quantum 520 image analysis system, damaged regions on the surfaces were examined. For each sample, microcracks in about l&20 viewfields of 0.025 mm’ each were counted and summed to reduce fluctuations resulting from mesoscopic inhomogeneities. Figure 3 shows the design and dimensions of the flyer used in the case study. Table 1 lists specifications of the test and relevant samples. Figure 4 shows the sequential pictures of microcracks on sectional surfaces of samples (co.1 ps, 0.26 ps, 0.5 ps and 0.8 ps, respectively)."
  }, {
